95,Towards a Data-Driven Approach for Early Identification of High-Risk Differentiated Thyroid Cancer Using Clinicopathologic Features,"Tahmima Hoque Eid, Ashim Dey",2026,"Abstract

Differentiated thyroid cancer (DTC) is primarily categorized into papillary and follicular types. It generally exhibits a good long-term prognosis, but some patients experience recurrence that adversely affects their health and treatment options. To facilitate the early detection of patients at greater risk, we propose an interpretable machine learning-based approach that combines domain-informed clinicopathologic encoding, foldwise handling of class imbalance, and ensemble learning with cross-validated model interpretation. We assessed multiple models across outer test folds, with the Bagging Classifier showing the best overall performance under nested cross-validation, yielding an accuracy of <tex xmlns:mml=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"" xmlns:xlink=""http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"">$\mathbf{9 6. 1 \%}$</tex> and an F1-score of <tex xmlns:mml=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"" xmlns:xlink=""http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"">$\mathbf{9 2. 9 1 \%}$</tex>. Moreover, we applied three diverse models using standardized <tex xmlns:mml=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"" xmlns:xlink=""http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"">$\mathbf{T}$</tex> and <tex xmlns:mml=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"" xmlns:xlink=""http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"">$\mathbf{N}$</tex> staging features and analyzed model decisions with SHAP. Nodal status (N) and tumor size (T) were the key staging predictors, exhibiting notable cross-interactions. They also interacted with clinical features such as Response and Risk, highlighting their combined association with recurrence risk. By integrating strong predictive performance with case-specific insights, this framework provides meaningful risk stratification and improves interpretability for healthcare practitioners. Before implementing this methodology in standard practice, multicenter validation and the inclusion of additional clinical biomarkers are essential.",https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/11546215/
